From a2090f18bd6dd81fcc7634b314e20dbb8ca81058 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GPenG Chen <302976981@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:28:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WifiService: Fix scan EOPNOTSUPP on drivers without
 SCAN_RANDOM_MAC_ADDR
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

createWiphyFeatures() used the NL80211_FEATURE_* constants (bit indexes,
e.g. 29/30) directly as bit masks, so (featureFlags & 29) actually tested
bits 0/2/3/4. Any driver that sets NL80211_FEATURE_SK_TX_STATUS (bit 0) —
e.g. the AIC8800 (rwnx) driver on the RK3576 Android 14 BSP kernel 6.1 —
was misdetected as supporting scan MAC randomization. WifiService then
sent NL80211_CMD_TRIGGER_SCAN with NL80211_SCAN_FLAG_RANDOM_ADDR, which
the kernel rejects with -EOPNOTSUPP because the driver never sets
NL80211_FEATURE_SCAN_RANDOM_MAC_ADDR. As a result every framework scan
failed and Settings showed no APs, while wpa_cli still worked since
wpa_supplicant does not request a random scan MAC.

Fix: shift the bit indexes to build the mask before testing. This also
fixes the same misdetection for scheduled scans (PNO).

Verified on ssi_17_arm64 fusion firmware (a17 system + a14 vendor,
kernel 6.1.172 + aic8800_fdrv): framework scans now succeed (144
results), TRIGGER_SCAN no longer carries RANDOM_ADDR and the kernel
no longer returns error 95.

Change-Id: Iaf6697269820fcc9f4b5827405d03c0bc9df0561
---
 .../java/com/android/server/wifi/nl80211/Nl80211Utils.java   | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/nl80211/Nl80211Utils.java b/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/nl80211/Nl80211Utils.java
index c90f275dcd..07a85487f5 100644
--- a/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/nl80211/Nl80211Utils.java
+++ b/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/nl80211/Nl80211Utils.java
@@ -2265,10 +2265,11 @@ public class Nl80211Utils {
     }
 
     private WiphyFeatures createWiphyFeatures(int featureFlags, byte[] extFeatureFlagsBytes) {
+        // NL80211_FEATURE_* constants are bit indexes, shift them to build the mask.
         boolean supportsRandomMacOneShotScan =
-                (featureFlags & NL80211_FEATURE_SCAN_RANDOM_MAC_ADDR) != 0;
+                (featureFlags & (1 << NL80211_FEATURE_SCAN_RANDOM_MAC_ADDR)) != 0;
         boolean supportsRandomMacSchedScan =
-                (featureFlags & NL80211_FEATURE_SCHED_SCAN_RANDOM_MAC_ADDR) != 0;
+                (featureFlags & (1 << NL80211_FEATURE_SCHED_SCAN_RANDOM_MAC_ADDR)) != 0;
 
         boolean supportsLowSpanOneShotScan = isExtFeatureFlagSet(extFeatureFlagsBytes,
                 NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_LOW_SPAN_SCAN);
